WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.768
Evaluation. Evaluation measures an AI system against defined expectations.

00:00:06.768 --> 00:00:16.224
Definition. It can assess task success, quality, latency, cost, safety, robustness, and user outcomes.

00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:24.768
Think of it like. You test normal operation, edge cases, and safety conditions before people depend on the result.

00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:34.872
How it works. Use representative tasks, expected outcomes, failure cases, and trace evidence to compare the system with its quality bar.

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:42.648
What it is not. The wrong record, a missed source, or a skipped human handoff can still make the system fail.

00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:50.112
Remember. Evaluation makes quality, risk, cost, and the next experiment explicit.
